.temp 27

* tb_sweep_follower.spice -- Stage A re-run (issue #295): output behaviour when
* both inputs are below / across the 1.20 V proposed ICMR floor.
*
* Unity-gain follower (VC tied to the inverting input FBN by a 0 V source), the
* non-inverting input swept 0 -> 1.5 V by `dc vin`. This is the DC-closed
* configuration that keeps the amplifier's output defined at every input level;
* it is NOT the consumer's type-III network (its C1/C2 are open at DC, so the
* consumer loop has no DC feedback path through the amplifier). The PWM-comparator
* gate approximation is on VC. DUT is the committed export; no transistor here.

.include '/tmp/buck-stage-a-4shji_tq/design.ngspice'
.include '/tmp/buck-stage-a-4shji_tq/opamp_two_stage.dut.spice'
.include '/tmp/buck-stage-a-4shji_tq/consumer_load.inc'

Vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
Ibias vdd ibias dc 10u
Vin vinp 0 dc 0
Vfb vc fbn dc 0
Xdut vdd 0 vinp fbn vc ibias opamp_two_stage
Xpwm vc pwm_in


.control
dc vin 0 1.5 0.05
option numdgt=7
wrdata /tmp/buck-stage-a-4shji_tq/sweep_follower.dat v(vc) v(xdut.tail)
.endc
.end
